    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u explain how lisinopril actually works in the raas pathway? i need to understand the specific steps for my exam",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Lisinopril functions as an ACE inhibitor, specifically blocking the Angiotensin-Converting Enzyme (ACE). ACE is responsible for converting inactive Angiotensin I into the potent vasoconstrictor, Angiotensin II. By inhibiting this enzyme, lisinopril prevents the production of Angiotensin II, leading to vasodilation and a subsequent decrease in blood pressure. This effectively lowers peripheral resistance within the Renin-Angiotensin-Aldosterone System (RAAS).",
      "source": "target",
